sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Order as Ordering Module
    participant Recipe as Recipe Module
    participant Inventory as Inventory Module
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Outbox as Outbox Relay
    participant Worker as Expiry/Recovery Workers (Slice 2E)
    participant Recon as Reconciliation/Admin (Slice 2E)
    participant MQ as RabbitMQ
    participant Analytics as Analytics Consumer

    Order->>Recipe: Calculate ingredient demand from order snapshots
    Recipe-->>Order: Ingredient quantities and recipe version
    Order->>Inventory: Convert(cartId, orderId, orderLines) at checkout (Slice 2D)

    Note over Inventory,DB: Begin local transaction
    Inventory->>DB: Lock the cart's ACTIVE holds (ascending cart item id)
    alt Nothing held (legacy cart line)
        Order->>Inventory: Demand calculated once through ConsumptionPlanService
        Inventory->>DB: Atomic conditional reserved_stock increment for that part only
    end
    Inventory->>DB: Copy the persisted cart snapshot into ONE order reservation
    Inventory->>DB: Mark each cart hold CONVERTED (order id, order line, target reservation)
    Note over Inventory,DB: Ownership moves as metadata: reserved_stock and current_stock do not move and no SALE_RELEASE is written
    Inventory->>DB: Insert InventoryReserved.v1 into outbox
    Note over Inventory,DB: Commit transaction
    Inventory-->>Order: Reservation ID

    Order->>Inventory: Consume(orderId) when the payment settles (Slice 2D)
    Inventory->>DB: Lock reservation by orderId
    alt Reservation is ACTIVE
        Inventory->>DB: Decrease current_stock and reserved_stock by the snapshot quantity
        Inventory->>DB: Insert exactly one immutable SALE_CONSUMPTION ledger transaction
        Inventory->>DB: Mark reservation CONSUMED
        Inventory->>DB: Insert InventoryConsumed.v1 into outbox
        DB-->>Inventory: Commit
    else Reservation already CONSUMED
        Inventory-->>Order: Idempotent success
    else Reservation not consumable
        Inventory-->>Order: 409 Invalid reservation state
    end

    opt Order cancelled or payment window expired before settlement
        Order->>Inventory: Release(orderId, ORDER_CANCELLED | PAYMENT_FAILED)
        Inventory->>DB: Lock reservation by orderId
        alt Reservation is ACTIVE
            Inventory->>DB: Decrease reserved_stock only
            Inventory->>DB: Insert one SALE_RELEASE ledger transaction
            Inventory->>DB: Mark reservation RELEASED
            Inventory->>DB: Insert InventoryReleased.v1 into outbox
            DB-->>Inventory: Commit
        else Reservation already RELEASED
            Inventory-->>Order: Idempotent success
        else Reservation already CONSUMED
            Inventory-->>Order: No automatic return; require waste or adjustment decision
        end
    end

    Note over Worker,DB: Slice 2E multi-node expiry and recovery (safe to run on every node at once)
    Worker->>DB: Claim expired ACTIVE order holds FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, stamp processing_owner/token/attempts (V047)
    alt Order is AWAITING_PAYMENT and not settled
        Worker->>DB: Expire the order and releaseOrder(ORDER_RESERVATION_EXPIRED) in its own transaction
    else Order payment is SETTLED but the hold is still ACTIVE (crash after settlement)
        Worker->>Inventory: PaidOrderRecoveryService.recover(orderId)
        alt All nine recovery conditions hold
            Inventory->>DB: consumeOrder — decrease current_stock and reserved_stock, one SALE_CONSUMPTION, mark CONSUMED
        else Ambiguous settlement
            Inventory-->>Worker: MANUAL_REVIEW — leave the hold untouched, never auto-release a paid order
        end
    else Payment ambiguous
        Worker->>DB: Skip now, reclaimable after the stale-claim window
    end
    Note over Recon,DB: Slice 2E reconciliation is a derived read; a dry run writes report rows only
    Recon->>DB: Scan derived reserved vs recorded balance and the join-based detectors
    Recon->>DB: Insert inventory_reconciliation_runs and inventory_reconciliation_findings (no balance or ledger write on a dry run)
    opt A repairable finding (cancelled-order hold, or a provably settled unconsumed order)
        Recon->>Inventory: repair(findingId) through the guarded primitive, revalidated live under lock
        Inventory->>DB: releaseOrder(DATA_RECOVERY) or consumeOrder — exactly one terminal ledger row, never both
    end
    opt Administrator releases one abandoned ACTIVE hold
        Recon->>Inventory: AdminReservationReleaseService.release(reservationId, expectedVersion, reason, idempotencyKey)
        alt Reservation is ACTIVE and in the caller's store scope
            Inventory->>DB: Decrease reserved_stock only, insert one SALE_RELEASE (ADMIN_RELEASE), mark RELEASED
        else CONSUMED or SETTLED or CONVERTED
            Inventory-->>Recon: 409 stable conflict
        end
    end

    Outbox->>MQ: Publish inventory events
    MQ->>Analytics: Deliver event
    Analytics->>DB: Deduplicate with consumer inbox and update projection

    Note over Inventory,DB: Available stock equals current_stock minus reserved_stock
    Note over Inventory,DB: One SALE_CONSUMPTION per reservation, enforced by uk_stock_consumption_reservation
    Note over Inventory,DB: Stock ledger rows are append-only and are not edited or deleted
